## 5. Charitable

- **No donor-advised fund.** The Coles give **$80,000 per year in cash** directly to their favourite charities.
- Meg **chairs a Dayton workforce-training nonprofit** and wants to **endow it with $5,000,000 during her lifetime**. She and David have not agreed and are still discussing it.
- No charitable technique of any kind is under consideration alongside the transfer structure.

**The 2026 arithmetic on the current giving.** Against roughly $5,000,000 of AGI, the OBBBA §170(b)(1)(I) floor disallows the first **$25,000**. Of $80,000 given, **$55,000** is deductible; at the 35% cap on itemized-deduction benefit the saving is **$19,250** — an effective subsidy of **24.06%**, not 37%. Illinois allows no charitable deduction at all.

